				{
					"name": "Refresh Token",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"auth",
								"refresh"
							]
						},
						"description": "Rotates authentication tokens using the presentation of the valid HTTP-only `refresh_token` cookie.\n\n### Mechanics\n- Reads `refresh_token` from request cookies.\n- Verifies JWT integrity and cryptographic SHA-256 hash match against active session in PostgreSQL.\n- **Replay Protection**: If a previously used refresh token hash is presented, the session is flagged as compromised and revoked immediately.\n- Upon validation, rotates the refresh token and issues a new access token, updating the cookies.\n\n### Cookies Sent\n- `refresh_token` (HTTP-only cookie)\n\n### Cookies Received\n- New `access_token`\n- New rotated `refresh_token`"
					},
